.TH OSP.PRECREATE_STATE 4 2026-09-18 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
osp.precreate_state \- history of object precreation stop and resume events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param osp." TARGET ".precreate_state"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR 444 " | " -r--r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per MDS OSP device connected to an OST.
.SH DESCRIPTION
An MDS keeps a pool of precreated objects on each OST so that file creation
does not have to wait for an
.B OST_CREATE
RPC. When the free space reported by an OST drops below
.BI "osp." TARGET ".reserved_mb_low"
or its free inode count drops below
.BI "osp." TARGET ".reserved_ino_low" ,
the OSP stops precreating objects on that OST, and resumes only once the
corresponding
.B reserved_mb_high
or
.B reserved_ino_high
watermark is crossed back.
.PP
The
.B precreate_state
parameter counts such transitions in each direction and reports the last 16
of them.
.BI "osp." TARGET ".prealloc_status"
reports the current state alone, so polling it shows neither when a
transition happened nor which space or inode value caused it.
.PP
Only watermark transitions are recorded. The history is not updated when
the OST cannot be used at all: the OSP has not connected yet, the import is
disconnected or deactivated, or an OST_CREATE RPC failed. Read
.BI "osp." TARGET ".prealloc_status"
for the error number, and
.BI "osp." TARGET ".state"
for the import state.
.PP
.B stop_count
and
.B resume_count
are the number of transitions in each direction since the OSP was started.
They are not reset when the history wraps, so they may be larger than the
number of entries listed.
.PP
.B state_history
is a YAML list whose entries each report the
.B time
of the transition in seconds since the epoch, its direction
.RB ( event ": " STOP " or " RESUME ),
the free space
.RB ( avail_mb )
and free inode count
.RB ( ffree )
seen at that moment, the four watermarks they were compared against, and the
target
.B state
flags, using the same letters as
.BR lfs-df (1).
.PP
Entries are only recorded on a transition, not while precreation stays
stopped. An OST that is out of space for a whole day produces one
.B STOP
entry, not one per statfs refresh.
.PP
Only the space and inode watermarks are tracked. A
.B RESUME
entry that still has the
.B N
flag means the watermark was crossed back, but object creation is separately
disabled by
.BI "obdfilter." TARGET ".no_create"
or
.BI "osp." TARGET ".max_create_count"
and does not resume.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B osp.*.precreate_state
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the precreation history of an OST that ran out of space and recovered:
.EX
.RB mds# " lctl get_param osp.testfs-OST0001-osc-MDT0000.precreate_state"
stop_count: 1
resume_count: 1
state_history:
 - { time: 1789012345, event: STOP, avail_mb: 812, reserved_mb_low: 1024, reserved_mb_high: 2049, ffree: 90210, reserved_ino_low: 32, reserved_ino_high: 65, state: "S" }
 - { time: 1789013901, event: RESUME, avail_mb: 3140, reserved_mb_low: 1024, reserved_mb_high: 2049, ffree: 90480, reserved_ino_low: 32, reserved_ino_high: 65, state: "" }
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B precreate_state
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_58-xx-gxxxxxxxxxx
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfs-df (1),
.BR lustre (7),
.BR lctl-get_param (8)
